MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_001: Eyes clear as running water, delicate lips upturned in\na coy smile... Yes, a beautiful drawing I've done.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_002: And now, the pale moon, it summons me out to a\nnight of sweetness. Off I go.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_003: I got so many nice perfumes! Can't wait to... Huh?
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_004: Goodness, Mu. Rather bold, dropping in on a man in\nthe middle of the night.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_005: What are you talking about? This is my room!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_006: The thrill of a good shopping trip can be quite\ndistracting, I know. But, ah—look around you?
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_007: Uh... Aah! You're right! These are your things,\nnot my things!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_008: Just so. Now, I must ask you to leave. This is well\npast bedtime for little girls.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_009: And I won't abide any whining. You're not so young\nyou can't sleep alone, are you?
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_010: Don't talk to me like I'm some kid. And, hey, you'd\nbetter not be off to see a woman. Go to bed!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_011: I know aaall about the portraits you draw of them\nin your notebook. Without asking!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_012: You do sketches of your targets, one after the other,\nand see a new one every night! It's kinda gross.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_013: Why, that's downright slanderous. My late-night\npursuits are for your good as well as mine.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_014: Hm. How do you figure?
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_015: Danger awaits at every turn of this journey!\nThere are bandit hideouts, deteriorated roads...
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_016: If we don't learn where such hazards are found,\nwe may lose our lives. I refuse to allow that.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_017: So, I tease out rumors from forthcoming ladies and\ndecide on a path forward. They act as my guides!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_018: Yeah but...spending the night with someone you\njust met. Isn't that dangerous?
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_019: Not if you mislead them with false vulnerability.\nBesides, I research them, and I can defend myself.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_020: Anyway, the moral of the story is—be wary of men\nwhispering sweet nothings. Good night, Mu.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_021: Yeah, great, thanks for the advice. You just think I'm\na kid anyway.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_C_022: Sirocco. Stupid jerk.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_001: I thought it was over that way. Hmm. Where is\nthis thing?
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_002: Looking for something? Or...you're lost! I can show\nyou the way back to the inn.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_003: Sirocco?! No, I'm not lost. And I told you to stop\ntreating me like a kid!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_004: There's no need to act tough around me. Though I\nsuggest you go back to the thoroughfare.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_005: Why? I was gonna go to the general store.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_006: H-heh... How kind for the answer to your question\nto appear before us.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_007: Haven't seen your mugs before. Not from around\nhere, eh? Gonna need some valuables from ya.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_008: Bandits! I-I-I don't have any valuables!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_009: Yes, that's right, thief. You picked the wrong marks.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_010: Ooh, you wanna go, huh? You're gonna wish you'd\nbehaved better.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_011: A thief has the temerity to lecture us on good\nbehavior? Inane. I'll have to teach you some sense.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_012: Whew. Thanks, Sirocco. But...how did you know\nthose guys were gonna show up?
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_013: I'd gotten hold of some information. I was coming\nhere to verify it when I happened to find you.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_014: Let me guess... You picked it up from some woman?
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_015: Indeed I did. But now you see, I'm not merely\nwomanizing.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_016: Yeah... I guess that notebook of yours really is for\ngathering information.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_017: {SetColor=Gray}That's so cool. He's like a spy! Doing all this stuff for\nespionage...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_018: You know, with that settled, I do believe this story\nwill make for some scintillating pillow talk!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_019: All the ladies awaiting the warm kiss of the wind...\nI must share it with them! A night of passion awaits!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_B_020: Huh? Sirocco! OK, he's definitely not perfect.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_001: Sirocco! Enemy at your back! Hyah!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_002: Nicely done, Mu! You've improved. But you must\nstill work on defending yourself! Hrah!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_003: Oh! Thanks for watching my back!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_004: Seems like the enemy's retreated. You're not hurt,\nare you?
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_005: Not at all, but— I don't know if I've said before how\nchanged you are.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_006: Your profile as you stride across the battlefield, your\ngraceful posture... There's no trace of the girl I met.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_007: OK, alright! You don't have to lay it on so thick.\nI know I still don't hold a candle to you.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_008: On the contrary, I think you're being modest.\nNot everyone can guard the Silver Hail's back.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_009: You've grown into a beauty who outshines the\nstars—and a reliable ally.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_010: What say you, Miss Mu? Shall we sit down\ntogether and gaze at the sunrise?
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_011: Hehe. I'll pass. Though as a kid I would have been\ndelighted.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_012: Besides, I know you've got others waiting for you.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_013: I won't deny it! But it would be rather tactless for\nme to discuss that with you.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_014: I see. I guess I won't need this then. Maybe I'll\nthrow it out.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_015: My notebook! How did that— When did you pilfer it\nfrom me?
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_016: It was sticking out of your pocket the whole fight.\nLooks like we both need to work on our defenses.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_017: Ha. The confidence it took to do that! You got the\nbetter of me.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_018: Yep—sorry. But I'll also say it's refreshing when you\ndrop the suave act.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_019: Now, I know you use the information from your\nwomanizing to help the rest of us...
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_020: but you also do it because you like it, right? I've seen\nthe gleam in your eyes when you're going out.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_021: Astutely observed! And such a far cry from when you\nwould interfere with my outings...
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_022: Alright, you've convinced me. Let's go somewhere\nand reminisce about the old days.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_023: You and your honeyed words! I'm fed up with them.\nBesides, a man gave me advice once.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_024: He said I had to be wary of men whispering\nsweet nothings.
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_025: Ohhh! You know how to hit me where it hurts.\nMy own words, come back to bite me!
MID_SE_Sci_Moo_A_026: Still, look at how skillfully you resisted being swayed!\nYou have become a delightful young woman.